# K9 Behavioral Architect — Design System

## Overview

**K9 Behavioral Architect** is an advanced AI-powered SaaS platform that unifies animal learning theory with clinical behavioral practice. Designed for **elite canine behaviorists and professional trainers**, it digests a high-value scientific corpus, transcripts, and webinar slides to structure, query, and deploy evidence-based behavioral modification protocols.

The product is a **single-surface technical dashboard** — a web application used by professionals who manage dogs, kennels, sessions, and behavioral protocols. Think of it as a command center for clinical canine science.

### Sources

- `uploads/DD-new_design_K9.md` — Design directive document specifying typography, colors, UI element rules, dark/light mode specs, and per-screen prompts.
- No Figma link or GitHub repo was provided. This design system is built from the design directive document above.

---

## Products

| Surface | Description |
|---|---|
| **App (Dashboard)** | Main SaaS product — multi-panel dashboard with sidebar nav, kennel/dog management, session logs, behavioral protocols, health tracking, AI query interface |

UI kit at: `ui_kits/app/`

---

## CONTENT FUNDAMENTALS

### Voice & Tone
- **Professional, clinical, precise.** This is a tool for experts — not a consumer app. Copy should feel like a well-designed scientific software product, not a pet startup.
- **Terse and functional.** Labels are short, action-oriented. No fluff, no exclamation marks.
- **Technical vocabulary is expected.** Terms like "behavioral modification protocol," "desensitization session," "reinforcement schedule," and "counterconditioning" are used without explanation.
- **No emoji** in UI. Status is communicated through color-coded badges and icons.
- **No first-person AI voice** ("I think..."). Results are presented factually.
- **English-first**, but Spanish is present in the design directive (the audience may be bilingual/international).

### Casing
- **Title Case** for navigation items, section headers, card titles.
- **Sentence case** for body text, descriptions, table values.
- **ALL CAPS** for status badges (e.g., "MISSING", "OFFLINE", "OK").
- **Monospace + uppercase** for kennel IDs, dog tags, session IDs.

### Example Copy Patterns
- "Health OK" / "MISSING" / "Offline" — status badges
- "Behavioral Modification Protocol" — section header
- "Save" / "Refresh" / "Reload" — action buttons
- "Session Log" / "Kennel Overview" / "Protocol Library" — nav labels

---

## VISUAL FOUNDATIONS

### Color System
| Role | Hex | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| **Primary Red** | `#ef4444` | Brand color — active nav items, primary buttons, selected states, logo accents |
| **Success Green** | `#10b981` | Health OK badges, active toggles, online status |
| **Warning Orange** | `#f59e0b` | Missing badges, offline states, alerts |
| **Dark BG (page)** | `#1a1b1e` | Dark mode page background |
| **Dark BG (card)** | `#25262b` | Dark mode card/panel backgrounds |
| **Dark Border** | `#373a40` | Dark mode card borders |
| **Light BG (page)** | `#f3f4f6` | Light mode page background |
| **Light BG (card)** | `#fefefe` | Light mode card/panel backgrounds |
| **Light Border** | `#e2e3e4` | Light mode card borders |

### Typography
| Role | Font | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| **Body / UI** | Space Grotesk | All body text, sidebar labels, nav, paragraphs, general UI labels |
| **Data / Dense** | JetBrains Mono | Small headers, calendar days, kennel names, data grids, status badges, IDs, dates |

Both fonts are available on Google Fonts (substituted from the design directive; originals assumed to be the same).

### Spacing & Radius
- **Corner radius:** `8px` (`rounded-lg`) on all cards, containers, panels
- **Borders:** `1px` solid, very subtle (uses dark/light border tokens)
- **Sidebar width:** ~220–240px
- **Card padding:** `16–24px`

### Backgrounds & Depth
- Two-level depth system: page background is darker than card background in both modes.
- No full-bleed background images or illustrations.
- No gradients on backgrounds. Clean flat surfaces.
- Very subtle `box-shadow` may be used on cards (low elevation).

### Sidebar Navigation
- Left sidebar: icon + text layout.
- Active item: red text + `rgba(239,68,68,0.1)` background tint (soft red).
- Inactive items: muted gray text, no background.
- Icons: minimalist stroke icons (Lucide/similar).

### Badges & Status Indicators
- **Pill-shaped** with a tiny colored dot inside.
- Text is uppercase, monospace font.
- Colors: green (OK/active), orange (missing/warning), red (critical/error), gray (inactive).

### Buttons
- **Primary:** Red background (`#ef4444`), white text, `8px` radius.
- **Secondary/Outline:** Transparent bg, gray text, subtle gray border. Hover changes border/text color.
- **Destructive:** Red outline or red-filled depending on context.

### Toggles
- Modern minimalist pill-shaped toggle.
- **Active:** Emerald green (`#10b981`) track, white knob.
- **Inactive:** Gray track, white knob.

### Animation & Interactions
- Minimal animation philosophy — functional transitions only.
- Hover states: slight opacity change or background tint on interactive elements.
- No bouncy or playful animations. Smooth, fast transitions (~150ms ease).
- Sidebar active state uses a soft background fill, not a hard border or underline.

### Dark vs Light Mode
- Dark mode is the **primary/preferred** mode — this is a technical dashboard.
- Light mode is a fully supported alternative.
- Cards always float above the page background in both modes.

### Imagery
- No decorative photography or illustrations mentioned.
- Data-driven visualizations (charts, grids, calendars) are the main "imagery."
- Color of data viz: uses brand primary/success/warning palette.

---

## ICONOGRAPHY

### Approach
- **Minimalist stroke icons** — consistent with Lucide Icons or similar (24px default, 16px in dense areas).
- No icon font built into the codebase; icons referenced via CDN (Lucide).
- No emoji used in UI.
- No PNG icons found — SVG stroke icons throughout.
- Icons appear in: sidebar navigation, status badges (dot only, no icon), button prefixes, data table actions.

### Icon System: Lucide Icons
- CDN: `https://unpkg.com/lucide@latest/dist/umd/lucide.min.js`
- Usage: `<i data-lucide="dog"></i>` with `lucide.createIcons()`
- Stroke weight: default (1.5px)
- Size: 18–20px for sidebar, 14–16px for inline/badge contexts

### Key Icons Used
| Context | Icon Name |
|---|---|
| Dogs / Animals | `dog`, `paw-print` |
| Kennel / Location | `home`, `map-pin` |
| Sessions / Calendar | `calendar`, `clock` |
| Protocols / Science | `flask-conical`, `brain` |
| Health / Status | `heart-pulse`, `activity` |
| Settings | `settings` |
| AI / Query | `bot`, `search` |
| Users | `user`, `users` |
| Reports | `bar-chart-2`, `file-text` |

